4.032><c>to </c><00:00:04.034><c>approximate </c><00:00:04.036><c>a  </c><00:00:04.038><c>function </c><00:00:04.040><c>on </c><00:00:04.042><c>the </c><00:00:04.044><c>entire </c><00:00:04.046><c>real </c><00:00:04.048><c>line </c><00:00:04.050><c>well  </c><00:00:04.052><c>that's </c><00:00:04.054><c>where </c><00:00:04.056><c>the </c><00:00:04.058><c>Fourier </c><00:00:04.060><c>transform </c><00:00:04.062><c>comes  </c><00:00:04.064><c>in </c><00:00:04.066><c>and </c><00:00:04.068><c>if </c><00:00:04.070><c>you're </c><00:00:04.072><c>interested </c><00:00:04.074><c>in </c><00:00:04.076><c>knowing  </c><00:00:04.078><c>about </c><00:00:04.080><c>that </c><00:00:04.082><c>then </c><00:00:04.084><c>I </c><00:00:04.086><c>will </c><00:00:04.088><c>see </c><00:00:04.090><c>you </c><00:00:04.092><c>in </c><00:00:04.094><c>my  </c><00:00:04.096><c>next </c><00:00:04.098><c>video</c>

